<title>UK: Sierra Leone added to war risks insurance clauses.</title>
<headline>Sierra Leone added to war risks insurance clauses.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The War Risks Rating Committee said it has agreed that sailings and flights to Sierra Leone should be subject to cargo war and strikes risks (marine and air) insurance clauses with effect from Thursday June 5 at 1600 hours GMT.</p>
<p>It added that voyages to the West African country would be held covered and rated at underwriters' discretion.</p>
<p>Held covered means not all war risk insurers will offer quotes. Shipowners must apply for cover and negotiate premiums with insurers for each voyage.</p>
</text>
